   "id": 532530,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the area of the trapezoid shown.<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/23dceac7a26af700.png\" alt=\"A trapezoid with its top and bottom sides marked 16 inches and 6 inches. The left and right sides are marked 13 inches. The height is marked 12 inches.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The area of a trapezoid with height <i>h</i> and parallel bases <i>a</i> and <i>b</i> is <span data-math=\"A = \\frac{1}{2}h(a + b)\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = \\frac{1}{2}h(a + b) = A = \\frac{1}{2}\\left( {{\\rm{12\\ in}}} \\right)(6{\\rm{\\ in}} + 16{\\rm{\\ in}}) = \\left( {6{\\rm{\\ in}}} \\right)\\left( {22{\\rm{\\ in}}} \\right) = 132{\\rm{\\ i}}{{\\rm{n}}^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>The area is 132 square inches.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"132\\,{{\\text{in}}^2}\">132\\,{{\\text{in}}^2}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
